==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Wall Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Eraser Cat''' when obtained from the [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Tank Maniac Stage]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Tank Cat is one of the most important meatshields in the game. She is similar to her [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|normal counterpart]] but with more versatility and ease of use thanks to her notably increased movement speed. Just like Tank Cat, she can be spammed to halt the progression of the enemy frontline towards the [[Cat Base]], making her an essential choice as a meatshield of many early game lineups.

Like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], being a fast meatshield brings multiple benefits; she can quickly protect Cat Units that are far from the cat base, it's easier for her to enter the blind spot of enemies with [[Long Distance]] attacks, and she won't linger in the battlefield for long and die faster from tanking hits. Therefore, she also won't clog up the cat deploy limit as much as slower meatshields. However, there will have a larger gap between each Crazed Tank Cat, creating a thinner line of defense compared to slower meatshields like the original Tank Cat.

Once you unlock her, you could use her to replace one of your other meatshields, as her HP is much higher than a Tank Cat which doesn't have many + levels. However, to cover gaps in her meat shielding, it is more effective to use her in tandem with the original to create a very thick line of defense, in a strategy known as Dual Erasers. This meatshield duo is extremely dominant across Stories of Legend, and can hold off the vast majority of threats at that stage of the game.

While enemies strong enough to kill her in one hit start appearing later in the game, this doesn't invalidate her usage. She can take good hits from peons, so it's advised to pair her with other meatshields, particularly ones that can take a hit even from the aforementioned stronger threats, like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and other slow specialist meatshields.

It's definitely worth it to hypermax her with [[Catseye]]s, as at high enough levels she can tank more hits from strong enemies like [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and [[R.Ost]], which can potentially make all the difference in winning the battle as she keeps other Cat Units alive for much longer.

==='''True Form'''===
Manic Eraser Cat gains more health and speed. Her health increases by about ~20% and her speed increases by 4. This may seem small, but it is a very, very great addition to her meatshield class. Manic Eraser's faster speed allows her to reach the the frontline faster and her increased health make her more bulky than she already was. A very great true form that makes her an even better meatshield for her price.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

