==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Crazed Wall Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[The Crazening (Removed Combo)|The Crazening]].
*In the Taiwanese version, Manic Eraser Cat doesn't have the word "NEKO" on its body. The same also applies to [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]].
*Crazed Tank Cat's storage icon is flipped. While virtually every other Cat's icon faces left, Crazed Tank Cat faces right.
*According to [https://x.com/tamasanp/status/1837422123968876562 a Twitter post] by art director Tamasan, Crazed Tank Cat only received arms because their design looked bland with only the pattern.
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Crazed Tank's description states her gender to be female, just like her regular counterpart.
*Crazed Tank Cat won the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=68aULQpEZBM 2025 Best Defender Nyaward], with a speech accompanying her victory:
<blockquote>
I don't think it's crazy to say that receiving this award is the biggest honor of my nine lives! Even though I've been chosen to take home this Nyaward, one cat standing alone can't hope to make a sturdy enough wall. Without Sushi Cat's maneuvers, Boogie's undefeatable cheer, or Rover's high-tech analysis, our army would be overrun in seconds! And I gotta give a shout out to my cousin Tank Cat for keeping me (mostly) sane during the fiercest battles! No matter how long this cat campaign will continue, I vow the cat base will continue to be safe in our paws! Nyank you!
</blockquote>
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Crazed Tank Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Crazed Tank Cat
Tough. High health. (Area Attack)
Strong enough to move a pebble.
Crazed version grants godspeed.</pre>
<pre>Crazed Wall Cat
Rigid defense. Now with corners. (Area Attack)
Strong enough to move a small rock.
Crazed version grants godspeed.</pre>
<pre>Manic Eraser Cat
Can take a beating thanks to elasticity.
Manic version grants even more
Really Good ™ Defense. (Area Attack)</pre>

